<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Corupedium</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">281 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-the-diadochi">Wars of the Diadochi</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Corupedium was fought in 281 BCE in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucus-i-nicator">Seleucus I</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lysimachus">Lysimachus</a>, two of Alexander's successors. Lysimachus was killed, and Seleucus gained control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a>. It was the last battle among Alexander's original generals and brought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> to its greatest extent.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-corupedium.jpg" alt="Battle of Corupedium" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jona Lendering · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plain_of_Corupedium.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
